WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.240
Over three years ago, I quit
my job as a pentester for Bug

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.480
Bounty and creating content.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.120
Unfortunately, the first two
years of Bug Bounty weren't as

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.480
easy as I expected them to be.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.240
But last year, the 2024, I really
changed a lot, and I succeeded

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.880
at least by my standards.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.000
In this video, I will tell you exactly
what I changed, what it takes to

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.280
succeed in Bug Bounty, and, as always,
I will share with you All the numbers.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.960
Enjoy.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.720
First a quick recap of my history.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.680
If you want to see it in details, you
can watch the past bounty vlogs, but

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.400
I'll just quickly mention what happened.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.560
In 2021,

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.040
I started hunting and I had
a few findings that year.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.360
Then 2022, it looked
like a really good start.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.240
I started hunting on more programs.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.160
I had multiple bounties.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:57.080
The year ended up with 21 paid bug
bounty reports totaling to about $24,000.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:01.560
And I think it was a good start,
especially considering that year I

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.640
spent a lot of time on the business
side, on the channel side, because I

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.480
also had to basically learn everything.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.480
But then it was 2023 and I

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.080
hoped to continue that trajectory.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:16.240
But that year it was really bad.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.560
if you watch the previous bounty vlog,
it didn't look as bad, but part of

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:27.640
it was because it didn't cover the
calendar year of 2023, but the period

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.920
that also had some bugs from 2022.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.520
But if we look at 2023 itself, I only
had five paid bug bounty reports.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:41.880
And yes, one of them was paid $20,000
so it didn't look as bad, but five

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.320
bug bounty reports in the whole year.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:49.760
Yes, it was a difficult year for me
personally, but five, what was I doing?

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.720
I don't know, to be
honest, how it happened.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:55.040
And myself, I was
surprised with this number.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.360
So you can definitely see that.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.040
It wasn't an easy start for me.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:04.680
I am not a story of somebody who
just started bug bounty and started

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.960
finding bugs easily left and right.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.320
But I was very, motivated
to eventually succeed.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:16.560
I was learning new things all the
time, changing my approach, and

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.360
I think I finally got better.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.400
And I'm in a point where I'm
really, happy with how it went.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:30.440
the biggest change I've made in 2024 was
being an expert in one area of hacking.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:35.000
Because if at the end of 2023,
you would ask me, what is my

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.800
strongest area of hacking?

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:42.000
I would tell you I'm good at everything,
which is a nice way of saying there was no

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.760
area at which I was exceptionally good at.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.040
In 2024,

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.440
I spent a lot of time on authentication.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.120
And if we take a look at stats out of 41

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:59.400
paid background reports in 2024, as much
as 14 are account takeovers totaling

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:07.480
to over $55,000, And some of them
are typical redirect_uri oauth ATOs.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:12.440
There is one xss that I exploited as
an account takeover, but there's also

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:17.680
a lot of random bugs that don't even
have the name that were just very

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.520
specific to a particular functionality.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.960
And they are not a result of me
copy pasting somebody's methodology.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:29.280
It's just a result of me spending
time on auditing, probably

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.680
hundreds of authentication flows.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:36.280
On implementing authentication
flows myself tens of times and just

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.160
understanding each piece of it.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:43.880
And That's something I'm probably
the most proud of that this year.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:48.680
I not only executed attacks that
I've learned from other people,

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:53.080
but also I had the chance to take
some ideas that I've had in the

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.600
past and I thought they can work.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:58.600
And that year I proved
that they indeed work.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:01.520
And some of them I
documented in the archive.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:07.400
Feel free to to check them out and
I'm definitely going to continue

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.200
in 2025 focusing on authentication.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:15.360
I really enjoy hacking this
part of applications.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.960
I think the impact is great.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:24.240
and the payouts itself, I think 55K
for 14 reports is a very, good result.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:29.720
Quantity wise, my second most commonly
rewarded bug class in 2024 was

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:35.720
privilege escalation bugs, which I
wouldn't say is a part of my style.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:41.280
And even though I had 13 reports, which
is only one less than the ATOs I mentioned

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.640
before with privilege escalations

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:47.240
out of out of 13 reports, I
didn't even make 10 grand.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.360
So you see the average
bounty is way lower.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:57.600
And the reality is out of these 13
reports, three are just my preparation for

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:03.720
recording the interview with the privilege
escalation God named Douglas Day.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:07.440
And just when preparing for this
interview, I found a few myself.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:13.560
And then I had one day where I reported
seven in a single application and

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:15.720
there were a few others as well.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:20.080
So even though quantity wise,
there is, it's a big part.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.960
I wouldn't say that's a
good part of my methodology.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:27.040
I think there is a lot of privilege
escalations out there, but I wouldn't

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:30.000
say I'm especially good at it.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.880
And I wouldn't say I want to be good at it
because the thing is, I don't really enjoy

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:36.840
looking for privilege escalation bugs.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:41.240
And that's also one thing that I
learned last year that when you work

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:46.200
for yourself, like you do in Bug
Bounty, enjoyment of doing something.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:50.120
Is not only for the sake of enjoying
it, but it's also for the sake of

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:53.280
keeping you motivated because when
you have no boss, if you have no

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.400
motivation, you will just not work.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:59.640
You will just not put the time
which is essential in bug bounty.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:03.840
I think it's the most important
aspect of bug bounty is as simple

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.000
as just putting in the time.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:11.360
So I am not planning to focus
more on this bug class myself.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:17.200
However, in 2025, I would
like to start using some hack

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.600
bots, maybe written by myself.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.840
And I think privileged escalation
bugs would be something that I

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:29.120
would start with for to outsource
this to, to some AI hack bots.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.280
Cause I think it should be fairly easy.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.240
And I think there is a lot of
money on the table because I

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.360
know these bugs are everywhere.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:39.480
And it just, the matter of.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.640
sending enough requests to see them.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:46.680
So hopefully I will start looking
for privilege escalations, but

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:52.320
not spending the time myself, just
having the, hackbots do it for me.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.520
So if you look income wise, my
second most profitable bug class

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.600
this year were client side RCEs.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:03.640
Even though I only had three paid
reports in this bug class, it yielded

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:11.080
at me over $17,000 And I really enjoyed
looking for these bugs, although.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:11.280
To

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:15.080
look for them, you must have a
kind of specific functionality.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.960
So even though I like them and I'm going
to keep looking for them whenever I

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.080
can, I would not say it's going to be

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.400
a big part of my methodology
because it is very specific.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:30.400
So either this target can be
susceptible to this or not.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:35.440
So I wouldn't say that's something that
I'm going to focus on a lot next year.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:40.920
Maybe if I would, it would be more in
terms of target selection rather than

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:45.960
the actual hacking style in terms of
hacking style sort of the rest of the

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:51.480
bugs i've had There was a lot of I
would say infrastructure related bugs.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:57.040
So ssrfs, traversals, request
smuggling these bugs I have

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.280
to say, I really like them.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:03.840
And I think I should focus
more on them because I just

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.440
enjoy looking for these bugs.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:08.440
I think I could automate
some of the checks.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.960
Maybe I should look for some zero days.

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:14.840
And, also the impact of this bug is great.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:18.160
And this is my, resolution
for this year as well.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.200
Of course, I will

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.560
keep authentication

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:26.880
as my main bug class and I'm gonna
keep this as my priority, but then I

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:32.280
think I would like to spend more time
on these infrastructure related bugs.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:38.200
And this is definitely something that
I want to spend more time in 2025.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:43.440
In 2024, I also finally had some
opportunities to hack in the real world

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.960
and meet so many people in person.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:50.760
First, I became the HackerOne
ambassador for Poland and we took

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.400
part in the HackerOne World Cup.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:58.080
And in 2024, we advanced easily
through the elimination stage.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.600
We advanced from the group stage.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:02.920
We won the elite 16 round.

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:07.120
And personally I also had pretty good
rounds because in each of them I was

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:11.600
able to find highs or crits which
is a good achievement considering at

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:14.600
the first rounds you compete with 700

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:20.440
hunters and there is no dupe window so I
think I'm quite happy with the progress.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:23.640
I also am very happy to
see Poland team succeed.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:26.800
I think before this, we
didn't have the community.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:32.120
So it's really nice to see how many
cool bugs we found during this round.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:35.200
But then individually, I also
had the chance to participate in

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:40.040
two HackerOne life hacking events
in Las Vegas and in Edinburgh.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:43.440
And it was amazing because
I met so many people that

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:48.480
I've known for years, but only from
the internet, only from online.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:53.720
And it was great to speak with them
also findings wise, also both LHEs I

00:09:53.720 --> 00:10:00.400
had highs, but even better in Edinburgh,
I was chosen for the show and tell for

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:05.560
those of you who don't know, show and tell
is the presentation at the life hacking

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:10.880
event where the customer chooses the most
interesting bugs to be shown on stage.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:16.840
imagine me seeing so many people in
the room that I just looked up to as

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:22.280
my authorities and they all listened to
me explaining my back from the stage.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:25.840
It was truly incredible
feeling and probably one of

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:28.960
my favorite moments of 2024.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:30.680
So it was really, nice.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:36.800
And just by hanging out with the top
hunters in the world, you simply absorb

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:40.520
the knowledge from everyone by just
talking with them and you understand

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:44.680
better and better what it actually
takes to succeed in bug bounty.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:50.400
I would say for me that the biggest lesson
is that at this level, everyone has a

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:53.560
very, good technical knowledge, but it's

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:54.920
finding the applications.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.320
That's the hard part.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:59.800
Sometimes it's just doing good
recon, but other times everyone

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:03.320
knows the application, but one
person, maybe they bought the

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:05.680
subscription and bypassed the paywall.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:09.920
Maybe they just figured out
better how to use certain feature.

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:15.280
Maybe they got verified and they have
access to endpoints that nobody else has.

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:19.920
Or sometimes, it's just out there
and nobody focuses on it because

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:23.040
they assume it is not insecure.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:25.600
So this is the biggest lesson for me.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:29.960
It's a very good way to put it is how
Douglas wrote it in his blog post.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:33.520
Finding bugs is easy,
finding scope is hard.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:37.000
For me, this one of the biggest
lessons of this year as well,

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.080
because I see from my bugs as well.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:45.560
In the past two years, I had the
technical knowledge to find most of them.

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:47.280
But still I didn't.

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:51.040
And the reason was putting in
the time and just being in the

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:53.560
correct place at the correct time.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:55.760
So maybe that's the case for you as well.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:12:00.600
Maybe you do already have the technical
knowledge to find bugs in bug bounty

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:04.400
and the only thing you need is the
persistence and going through enough

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:09.720
programs, going through enough websites
and going through enough endpoints

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:12.520
Here comes the moment
you've all been waiting for.

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:13.840
The numbers.

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:17.240
First, for reference, here
we have the numbers from

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:29.200
Past two years and the total of my
bounties for 2024 is $96,347 and 67 cents.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:33.160
I still have some mediations open,
and I hope I will actually cross the

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:35.800
$100k line, but even if I didn't,

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:36.520
I'm

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:40.520
really happy with this number, especially
that it's only part of my income.

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:44.840
I spend about three days
per week on average hacking.

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:52.000
So I know if I would focus 100 percent
of my time, I could easily cross the

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.520
100 K line and maybe even, higher.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:59.640
So I decided to put this in the
title, even though technically, at

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:02.240
least for this moment, it's not true.

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:06.000
If you think I'm an idiot for doing
this, leave the comment down below.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:09.240
If you think I'm not and you
enjoyed this video, also, I'm

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:10.640
waiting for all your comments.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:11.640
For now,

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:18.120
thank you so much for
watching and goodbye!

